params.body:
## What

A read-only command, `stocklist:rights-dry-run`, that shows per garage what would change if the garage's modules decided the menus instead of its users' roles. Nothing is written and no behaviour changes: this is the measurement that has to come before any enforcement.

```bash
php artisan stocklist:rights-dry-run                          # model, summary, losses per menu, the active garages that lose
php artisan stocklist:rights-dry-run --csv=/tmp/rights.csv    # plus one row per garage (semicolons, BOM, opens in Excel)
php artisan stocklist:rights-dry-run --garage='Garage V*'     # narrow by name (* is a wildcard) or by id
```

## Why

Menus come from `role_access` per role, and the three garage roles are combinations: "Dealers M1" (3), "Traders M2" (4), "Dealers en Traders" (5). What a customer bought lives on the garage (`module_1` own stock, `module_2` trade and biddings), and the two disagree: a garage can carry role 5 with both modules off, and role 5 is not the union of 3 and 4 (it grants menus neither has and lacks `user`, which both have). Moving the decision to the garage cannot be done blind; this run says, garage by garage, who would lose what and whether anybody there is still using the platform.

## The target model: `App\Support\GarageRights`

One place, meant to be reused by the enforcement step:

- **base** (every customer, at least one module on): what roles 3 and 4 both grant;
- **dealer** (`module_1`): what role 3 grants and role 4 does not;
- **trader** (`module_2`): what role 4 grants and role 3 does not;
- **gated menus** (`menus.ability`, today only transport via `use-transport`): decided by their Gate, the same answer before and after;
- **both modules off**: a stopped customer, none of the above;
- roles 1, 6, 7 and 8 are out of scope and keep what their role grants.

What **only role 5** grants is neither dealer nor trader, so the model does not place it: the command prints those menus under "they need a decision", and marks them per garage (`lost_needing_decision`). The sets are derived at run time from what roles 3, 4 and 5 grant, so the output reflects production as it is. Only the view right is modelled; add, edit and delete stay on the role row.

## Per garage: `App\Support\RightsDryRun`

Garages with at least one user in roles 3, 4 or 5; demo garages (`is_demo_user`) and staff accounts (`%stocklistdealer%`, the insights filter) left out. For each: modules, the roles of its users, the menu set today (union over its users' roles, view = 1) against the target, menus lost and gained, number of users, last sign-in (`activity_events`) and page views in the last 30 days (`activity_page_views`), own stock (the `StockInsights::OWN_STOCK` definition) and the last car created and sold. `vehicles.updated_at` is not used: the cutover of 15 September touched every row.

Classes: `unchanged`, `gains only`, `loses menus - active`, `loses menus - dormant`, `both modules off - active`, `both modules off - dormant`. Active means a sign-in or a page view in the last 30 days. Both logs started on 25 September 2026, so "dormant" means nothing since then; the command prints from which date it could see.

## Read-only is structural

The whole run goes through `App\Support\ReadOnlyRun`, which looks at every statement on the connection before it is sent and refuses anything that is not a read with an exception. A later edit that adds a write to this path fails instead of writing. The only output besides the terminal is the CSV file, when asked.

## Tests

`RightsDryRunTest` (menus with keys of their own, so the assertions hold whatever the role table already carries):

- the model: base, dealer and trader split from roles 3 and 4; a role-5-only menu is listed as undecided and granted by no module; both modules off gives nothing;
- a role-5 garage without modules that signed in 3 days ago is `both modules off - active`; with its last sign-in 45 days ago it is `both modules off - dormant`;
- a role-4 garage (whose role lacks the stock list) with both modules on gains the stock list through `module_1` and loses nothing: `gains only`;
- a role-3 garage with `module_1` only is `unchanged`;
- a role-5 garage with both modules loses the role-5-only menu, gains `user`, and is active on page views alone: `loses menus - active`;
- a role-3 garage on a trader-only garage without activity: `loses menus - dormant`;
- demo garages and garages without a combination role are left out;
- the command leaves `dealers`, `users`, `role_access`, `menus`, `roles`, `activity_events`, `activity_page_views` and `vehicles` identical (count and a hash of every row) and writes the CSV;
- a write inside `ReadOnlyRun` is refused and never reaches the table, and the guard is off afterwards.

## Business rules

No behaviour changes, so no rule changes. There is no open point on roles or rights in `docs/bedrijfsregels/open-punten/`; the related rule is R S4-10.18 (transport as a garage switch, the first menu decided by a Gate), which this model keeps as is.
